# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the multithreaded API tests (test/api/mt,
# label "mt"; preset tsan-mt, workflow tsan-mt.yml).
#
# Each entry is a known race of the engine built with
# ZORBA_FOR_ONE_THREAD_ONLY=OFF, under a "# <inventory ids> (P<n>): ..."
# comment that names its ids in the inventory of the thread-safety design and
# the PR of its plan that removes it (the workflow's summary reads that
# comment). The PR that fixes a race deletes its entries, so the job then
# fails if the race is still there; a race not listed here fails its test.

# S3 (P2): QNameItem::free releases the item lock that removeReference
# already released.
mutex:zorba::simplestore::QNameItem::free

# S7 (P7): ContentReader keeps one unsynchronized table of open iterations
# for the whole process.
race:zorba::simplestore::ContentReader::

# R1 (P3): SimpleRCObject counts are plain integers in every build (builtin
# function objects, TypeManager, plan iterators shared by clones).
race:zorba::SimpleRCObject::addReference
race:zorba::SimpleRCObject::removeReference
race:zorba::SimpleRCObject::getRefCount

# R1, R2 (P3): a Schema freed while another thread uses it, after a count of
# its TypeManager or of a user-defined XQType raced.
race:zorba::Schema::

# C1 (P9): user function plans are generated lazily by the first call, on the
# user_function object that every clone shares.
race:zorba::user_function::getPlan

# C4 (P9): rewrites of one compilation annotate expressions that another
# compilation owns (functions of a shared static context).
race:zorba::MarkFreeVars::apply
race:zorba::expr::set*(zorba::BoolAnnotationValue)

# C8 (P8): every open() writes the iterator's state offset into the shared
# plan.
race:zorba::StateTraitsImpl<*>::createState

# C9 (P8): openImpl writes static and dynamic context values into members of
# the shared iterator.
race:zorba::CompareIterator::openImpl
race:zorba::ElementIterator::openImpl

# C10 (P9): rewrites set flags on FLWOR expressions that clones share.
race:zorba::flwor_expr::set_general

# G2 (P10): dict::find initializes its begin and end pointers lazily.
race:zorba::diagnostic::dict::find
